WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.846 --> 00:00:02.704
A plant is building a new hall.

2
00:00:03.407 --> 00:00:07.866
Packing line 3 has to move there, during the summer shutdown of 3 weeks.

3
00:00:08.885 --> 00:00:12.554
Every project walks the same road, past five stations.

4
00:00:13.698 --> 00:00:17.901
At each station you see what happens, and what goes wrong if you skip it.

5
00:00:19.266 --> 00:00:21.286
The first station is the intake.

6
00:00:22.013 --> 00:00:24.114
The request is, move line 3.

7
00:00:24.817 --> 00:00:27.372
You dig deeper, to the question behind it.

8
00:00:28.142 --> 00:00:30.475
Why does it have to happen, and when is it done?

9
00:00:31.477 --> 00:00:34.994
The answer becomes the goal, what must be measurably different.

10
00:00:35.782 --> 00:00:40.484
After the shutdown line 3 runs in hall B, as fast as it does now.

11
00:00:41.158 --> 00:00:44.827
The sponsor owns the budget and the result, and decides.

12
00:00:45.915 --> 00:00:48.899
Skip the intake, and you may solve the wrong problem.

13
00:00:50.199 --> 00:00:51.883
The second station is Plan.

14
00:00:52.587 --> 00:00:55.698
You turn the goal into a plan that people believe in.

15
00:00:56.683 --> 00:00:59.865
The work, the order, the duration and the risks.

16
00:01:00.580 --> 00:01:03.169
The intro of Plan shows them one by one.

17
00:01:04.144 --> 00:01:07.186
Without a plan you only notice in the last week of the

18
00:01:07.267 --> 00:01:10.390
shutdown itself that the new power supply is not ready.

19
00:01:11.068 --> 00:01:12.403
Then it is too late.

20
00:01:13.750 --> 00:01:15.364
The third station is Run.

21
00:01:16.125 --> 00:01:18.226
Now the project has to keep moving.

22
00:01:19.267 --> 00:01:20.730
With an honest status.

23
00:01:21.419 --> 00:01:26.202
The switchboard will arrive later than planned, so you set the status to amber now.

24
00:01:27.237 --> 00:01:30.209
Someone asks whether line 4 can come along too.

25
00:01:30.945 --> 00:01:35.508
That becomes a change request, and the sponsor chooses in the steering group.

26
00:01:36.545 --> 00:01:39.169
Without steering you get a watermelon project.

27
00:01:39.890 --> 00:01:43.559
Green outside, red inside, until it is too late.

28
00:01:44.945 --> 00:01:46.605
The fourth station is Land.

29
00:01:47.453 --> 00:01:51.806
Line 3 is in place, and now the new way of working has to stick.

30
00:01:52.818 --> 00:01:56.800
The operators get a work instruction with photos of the real line,

31
00:01:56.998 --> 00:01:58.438
and training on the floor.

32
00:01:59.464 --> 00:02:00.962
Then the line takes over.

33
00:02:01.677 --> 00:02:02.908
It is about adoption.

34
00:02:03.606 --> 00:02:07.054
People work the new way, even when nobody is watching.

35
00:02:08.090 --> 00:02:12.211
Skip this, and the result slips back a few months after the project.

36
00:02:13.542 --> 00:02:15.446
The last station is Close.

37
00:02:16.166 --> 00:02:18.511
The work is done, the project is not.

38
00:02:19.573 --> 00:02:23.660
You measure the line the same way as in the baseline, from before the move.

39
00:02:24.405 --> 00:02:25.833
Then the sponsor signs.

40
00:02:26.946 --> 00:02:28.293
Then a retrospective.

41
00:02:29.018 --> 00:02:32.175
What do we repeat, and what do we do differently next time?

42
00:02:33.170 --> 00:02:36.235
Without closing, nobody knows whether it worked.

43
00:02:37.018 --> 00:02:39.874
And the next project makes the same mistakes.

44
00:02:41.185 --> 00:02:42.857
This is the map of Projects.

45
00:02:43.573 --> 00:02:46.185
The five stations lie on one road.

46
00:02:46.933 --> 00:02:49.336
Around it lie the other parts of the field.

47
00:02:50.455 --> 00:02:53.799
First the intake and Plan, the question and the plan.

48
00:02:54.860 --> 00:02:57.577
Then Run and Land, the work and the change.

49
00:02:58.601 --> 00:03:00.877
Finally Close, proving and learning.

50
00:03:01.893 --> 00:03:04.691
Each station is a module with four topics.

51
00:03:05.413 --> 00:03:06.667
Start with the intake.
